.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-step-env 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-step\-env \- Print the sorted `env` lines a declared environment keys, the step cache\*(Aqs answer to the tool line
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten step env\fR [\fB\-\-exclude\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIpatterns\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the sorted `env` lines a declared environment keys, the step cache\*(Aqs answer to the tool line
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-exclude\fR \fI<exclude>\fR
A variable a pattern matches that is never keyed, such as a per\-run pid (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIpatterns\fR>
The names or PREFIX* patterns, after `\-\-`: an `env NAME=value` line per keyed variable, `env PATTERN none` where none matches
